    }
  ],
  "caveats": "Figures are territorial (production-based) CO2 emissions from fossil fuel combustion, cement, and other industrial processes; they exclude land-use change/LULUCF emissions and are NOT adjusted for trade (consumption-based accounting would shift emissions from exporters like China toward importers like the US/EU). International aviation and shipping ('bunker fuels') are included only in the World total, not attributed to individual countries. The 2025 Global Carbon Budget's current-year figure for the most recent year is a projection at the time of publication and subject to later revision. Per-capita values use UN population estimates; cumulative figures are historical sums since 1750 and are sensitive to how far back the underlying series extends for each country. Country borders/entities follow OWID's current-day definitions, which can complicate long-run cumulative comparisons for countries that split or merged (e.g. USSR, Czechoslovakia)."
}
